===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} Damage to, disease of, or abnormality of the [[kidney]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-07-17|author=|title=The Addition of Vascular Calcification Scores to Traditional Risk Factors Improves Cardiovascular Risk Assessment in Patients with Chronic Kidney Disease|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0131707|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0131707|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=The recorded causes of kidney disease were as follows: diabetic '''nephropathy''' (in 21% of the patients), nephroangiosclerosis and glomerulonephritis (18%), interstitial '''nephropathy''' (7%), hypertensive '''nephropathy''' (5%), polykystosis (5%) and other recorded diagnoses (hereditary disease, solitary kidney, dysglobulinemia, and systemic disease) (22%).}}

